-- temples ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- every column of public.temples is listed here, in schema order, so this seed
-- is a complete picture of the table rather than a partial one: re-running it
-- also resets anything an earlier run wrote. the two keys (id, temple_id) are
-- the only columns absent from the on conflict set below, because they are the
-- keys it matches on.
--
-- cover_image holds a Wikimedia Commons url and every temple also gets temple_images
-- rows at the bottom of this file. an earlier version of this seed left both empty
-- on purpose, because public/assets holds no temple photographs and a url that
-- resolves to nothing renders a broken frame in the hero and on every card. that
-- reasoning still holds for a locally invented url, which is why the photographs
-- used here were fetched and confirmed to be real images before being written down
-- rather than typed in from memory.
--
-- country is written out rather than left to the column default. the default
-- ('India') is still the right value, but a seed that spells it out is a seed
-- the reader can diff against a row an admin edited, and the mapper also
-- defaults a null country to 'India', so the two cannot disagree.
--
-- updated_at mirrors added_at here. a seeded row has never been edited, and a
-- fresh timestamp on every re-run would make the whole table look churned.
--
-- the seven timing columns and temple_festivals are all new since the first
-- version of this seed. the old single `timings` string is gone: it
-- could not say which day a visitor was asking about. the old special_days blob
-- moved into temple_festivals below, one row per festival with a real date.
insert into public.temples (
  id, temple_id, name, name_ta, deity, cover_image,
  address, city, district, state, country, maps_url,
  history,
  sunday_timings, monday_timings, tuesday_timings, wednesday_timings,
  thursday_timings, friday_timings, saturday_timings,
  contact, whatsapp, email, contact_person, website,
  is_approved, active, added_at, updated_at
