-- temple_festivals -------------------------------------------------------------
-- one row per festival, replacing the single temples.special_days text blob. every
-- temple is seeded with five of them so the festival panel on the public page is
-- populated for all five, including the unpublished one.
--
-- the dates here are 2027 because temple and temple festival dates follow the lunar
-- calendar and move every year; the public page hides anything whose date has
-- passed, so these are next season's dates rather than ones that read as
-- already over.
--
-- happens_on is left null on one row per temple on purpose. a temple often knows
-- the festival is happening before it has fixed the date, and that state has to
-- render as the name alone rather than vanish. the public query keeps these and
-- sorts them last, so they do not push a dated festival off the top.
--
-- one row per temple carries a date already in the past, so the date filter is
-- exercised in both directions: it stays visible in the admin, where the operator
-- rolls it forward to next year, and is hidden from visitors. tmpl-3 carries it.
