-- temple_images ----------------------------------------------------------------
-- the gallery rows for the cover urls set above. every url is a Wikimedia Commons
-- file that was requested and answered with an image content-type before being
-- written here, so none of these can be a 404 or an html error page dressed up as a
-- photograph. they are hotlinked, not copied: this stays a text seed, and the
-- original file is freely licensed. author and licence for each one are on that
-- file's Commons page, named by the url itself.
--
-- the cap is four rows per temple, not five: enforce_temple_image_cap() counts
-- temples.cover_image as one of the five, so a cover plus four gallery rows is the
-- maximum and a fifth insert raises. tmpl-3 has three confirmed photographs, so it
-- takes two gallery rows and ends on three images rather than padding to the cap
-- with a picture of the wrong temple.
--
-- sort_order is the order the admin panel and the lightbox walk, so it starts at 0
-- and ascends from the strongest view of the building. the cover is deliberately
-- repeated as the first gallery image: the gallery component takes the first row as
-- its hero source, and the admin cover picker expects row 1 to be that same shot.
--
-- this delete runs first, before the insert, and it is what makes the section
-- idempotent. the cap trigger counts the rows already present, so re-running the
-- insert alone would hit the five-image ceiling on the last temple and fail the
-- whole seed. scoped to the five temples this file owns, so an image an admin
-- uploaded for some other temple is untouched.
delete from public.temple_images where temple_id in ('tmpl-1', 'tmpl-2', 'tmpl-3', 'tmpl-4', 'tmpl-5');

